---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HousingRequest from '../components/HousingRequest.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { u } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  title="Housing and Residential Life"
  description="Residence halls, Spring Semester 2027 move-in, and how to request a repair at the University of Mars."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Campus Life"
    title="Housing &amp; Residential Life"
    lede="Most first-year students live on the Jezero campus. Fall 2026 contracts run through Spring Semester 2027."
    crumbs={[{ href: '/housing/', label: 'Housing' }]}
  >
    <p class="page-actions">
      <button class="btn call-launch" type="button" data-call-launch="housing">Call Housing Support</button>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={u('/support/?category=housing-repair#request')}>Request a repair</a>
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="prose wrap">
    <div class="media-block">
      <div class="frame">
        <Photo
          name="residence-halls"
          alt="Residence halls around a courtyard at sunset, with string lights and a red ridge beyond."
          sizes="(min-width: 800px) 36rem, 100vw"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="halls">Residence halls</h2>
        <p>
          A standard double with a meal plan is budgeted at $16,480 for the 2026–27 academic year. Assignments for
          students new this spring were posted in MyUM in December.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hall-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Olympus Mons Hall</h3>
        <p>First-year traditional rooms, south quad. 420 beds. Staffed desk until midnight.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Isidis Hall</h3>
        <p>First-year and second-year suites, east of the library. Shared kitchen on each floor.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Syrtis Court</h3>
        <p>Upper-division apartments on the north edge of campus. Nine-month and twelve-month contracts.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Elysium Hall</h3>
        <p>Upper-division singles and doubles in the west village. Quiet house by agreement.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h2 id="move-in">Move-in</h2>
    <p>
      Fall move-in was Saturday and Sunday, August 22–23, 2026. Most continuing students keep their keys through winter
      break and do not move out between semesters.
    </p>
    <p>
      Spring Semester 2027 move-in for students with a new spring assignment was Saturday, January 2, and Sunday,
      January 3, 2027, from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. at the hall desk. Students who have not checked in should call the hall desk
      before they arrive. Bring a photo ID. Cars may stop on the service drive for 20 minutes.
    </p>
    <p>Quiet hours are 10 p.m. to 8 a.m. Sunday through Thursday, and midnight to 8 a.m. Friday and Saturday.</p>

    <h2 id="repairs">Maintenance</h2>
    <HousingRequest />
    <p>
      For a dripping tap, a light, a heater that is uneven, or furniture that failed, submit a housing repair. The form
      above calls housing support, or the Help Center form opens with that category already chosen.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={u('/support/?category=housing-repair#request')}>Open the repair form</a>
      with the housing category already selected.
    </p>
    <p>
      Routine work is scheduled on weekdays. You will get a note at your UM email when the ticket is assigned. See the
      <a href={u('/support/articles/housing-repair/')}>housing repair article</a> for what to include.
      Booked repairs are listed on the <a href={u('/housing/work-orders/')}>facilities schedule</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="emergency">Emergency repairs</h2>
    <p>
      Call <a href={site.repairHref}>{site.repairPhone}</a> at any hour for an active leak, no heat when the night will
      be unsafe, a power loss in the whole unit, or a door that will not secure. Do not use the online form for those.
    </p>
    <p>
      Housing office: <a href={site.housingHref}>{site.housingPhone}</a>,
      <a href={`mailto:${site.housingEmail}`}>{site.housingEmail}</a>. Weekdays, 9 a.m. to 4 p.m., Isidis Hall, Room 10.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
